From 98f02d611b4f13b99490dbe49476df500a4404f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvia420-bit <salvia420@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:22:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] fix(economy): fix R2-HIGH-01/02 and R2-MED-01 siege &
 bullion rollback bugs

- [R2-HIGH-01] Pre-check player burden capacity in IndustryManager.TryMintBullion before consuming stock, add TownEconomyManager.RefundWarehouseStock + ConsumedWarehouseSlice tracking so rollbacks restore exact slices additively without wiping warehouse stock or clearing InactivityElapsedSec.
- [R2-HIGH-02] Enforce Allegiance ownership parity and DoorProgress >= 0.8f on 0x0912 DepositSupply IsoContainerDeployable unloading, restrict standalone DeployableBase consumption in DepositSupply to owned CoreSampleCrate (4000074), and block non-cargo defense/grid/industrial/infrastructure deployables and unauthorized containers/units in ForwardSiegeBeaconDeployable.
- [R2-MED-01] Pre-validate via SiegeManager.CanDeliverSiegeSupply, consume inventory item and verify consumption return bool BEFORE calling TryAcceptProvenanceDelivery in ForwardSiegeBeaconDeployable.TryAcceptInventoryItem.
- Add Tier5_R2HIGH01, Tier5_R2HIGH02, and Tier5_R2MED01 adversarial tests in Tier5AdversarialE2ETests.cs.

Verified:
- ECONOMY_E2E_STRICT=1 dotnet test -c Debug --filter "FullyQualifiedName~Economy|FullyQualifiedName~VehicleWire" -> 157/157 passed
- dotnet test -c Debug --filter "FullyQualifiedName~Vehicles|FullyQualifiedName~Landblock" -> 367/367 passed
